flowchart TD
  Individual[Create and verify each transaction individually]
  Add[Add verified item]
  Manager[Review batch membership and order]
  Remove{Remove or edit an item?}
  Invalidate[Invalidate final verification and dependent approval]
  Validate[Backend validates exact batch and context]
  Valid{Batch valid and current?}
  Review[Review complete payload, account, chain, and contract]
  Consent[User explicitly initiates supported contract operation]
  Wallet[Wallet presents one supported contract call]
  Execute[Contract execution]
  Outcome{Execution outcome}
  Confirmed[Show confirmed result and audit reference]
  Partial[Show per-item outcome only if contract reports partial semantics]
  Failed[Show rejection, revert, or unknown status]
  Rebuild[Correct batch and request fresh validation]

  Individual --> Add --> Manager --> Remove
  Remove -->|yes| Invalidate --> Manager
  Remove -->|no| Validate --> Valid
  Valid -->|no or expired| Rebuild --> Individual
  Valid -->|yes| Review --> Consent --> Wallet --> Execute --> Outcome
  Outcome -->|confirmed| Confirmed
  Outcome -->|partial, if supported| Partial
  Outcome -->|rejected, reverted, pending, or unknown| Failed
  Failed --> Rebuild

  Note[One wallet approval means one contract call only when the deployed contract and wallet support it. Atomicity, limits, and partial failure are TBD.]
  Review -. limitation .-> Note
